<title>USA: Clinton proposes $260 mln, 5-yr tax cuts for D.C..</title>
<headline>Clinton proposes $260 mln, 5-yr tax cuts for D.C..</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration plans to propose $260 million worth of tax incentives for the District of Columbia over the the next five years, it said in a press statement.</p>
<p>The incentives would be designed to encourage employment of city residents and revitalize distressed areas. It gave no further details.</p>
